/T (Stage 4: Systems Diagnosis Armed with data from both sides; we mapped the full-service system, from student arrival and ordering through to food collection and seating. This mapping revealed multiple feedback loops: overcrowding slows service, which increases perceived wait time, which causes students to cluster near the counter, which further slows service. The system was locked in a vicious cycle with no corrective mechanism.)
/E (Stage 4: Systems Diagnosis Armed with data from both sides; we mapped the full-service system, from student arrival and ordering through to food collection and seating. This mapping revealed multiple feedback loops: overcrowding slows service, which increases perceived wait time, which causes students to cluster near the counter, which further slows service. The system was locked in a vicious cycle with no corrective mechanism.)
