/T (1. Gaining Stakeholder Buy-In: Convincing Cafe Adda's management to trial interventions, particularly the Buzzer System, required demonstrating the problem's scale in terms they found immediately relevant. Initial conversations focused on food quality, which management correctly identified as strong. Reframing the conversation around revenue leakage from lost customers and the measurable impact on repeat footfall was key to achieving cooperation.)
/E (1. Gaining Stakeholder Buy-In: Convincing Cafe Adda's management to trial interventions, particularly the Buzzer System, required demonstrating the problem's scale in terms they found immediately relevant. Initial conversations focused on food quality, which management correctly identified as strong. Reframing the conversation around revenue leakage from lost customers and the measurable impact on repeat footfall was key to achieving cooperation.)
